00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.170 align:start position:0%
EU ministers meeting in the  competitiveness Council on Thursday and  Friday will hold a debate on three  important topics first they will discuss  how to foster industrial competitiveness  to create new jobs and growth  recognizing that Europe is still far  from the twenty percent target of  industry share in Europe's GDP by 2020  the Commission urged member states to  mainstream industrial competitiveness  across all relevant EU policy areas such  as environment energy trade or regional  policies the outcome of the discussion  will feed into the debate on industrial  competitiveness to take place at the  next spring EU summit following the  first report on progress towards the  implementation of the European research  area EU ministers are also expected to  outline the key elements that will  contribute to the completion of the  research area by 2014 by creating a  unified research area where researchers  scientific knowledge and technology can  circulate freely the idea is to  strengthen Member States is scientific  and technological capacities to increase  growth and jobs in the long run on space  matters ministers will discuss how to  better work with the european space  agency to support the global  competitiveness of the european space  industry and allow it to unleash its  full potential
 

